          %h3#References References
          %p The main relation/application to quantum field theory is given by the following book, which also contains a careful introduction to the notion of factorization algebra.
          %ul
            %li [CG] K. Costello and O. Gwilliam, Factorization algebras in quantum field theory.
          %p An out-dated version is available on Costello’s webpage. Participants can also join our mailing list to get the most up-dated version.
          %p A more mathematical introduction to factorization algebra is given in
          %ul
            %li [Ginot] G. Ginot, Notes on factorization algebras, factorization homology and applications, arXiv:1307.5213[math.AT].
          %p A much more elaborated treatment (using slightly different languages from the formers):
          %ul
            %li
              [Lurie] J. Lurie, Higher Algebra.
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~lurie/papers/higheralgebra.pdf"} pdf
          %p The introduction to operads is based on
          %ul
            %li
              [LV] J.-L. Loday, B. Vallette: Algebraic Operads.
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://math.unice.fr/~brunov/Operads.html"} Pdf available here
          %p
            For
            %math#mathml_1eede68f8c470afbdd52f909556a007fbb3d6421_32.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            operads, see
          %ul
            %li
              [F] B. Fresse: Introduction to
              = succeed "-operads" do
                %math#mathml_1eede68f8c470afbdd52f909556a007fbb3d6421_33.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_n
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://www.newton.ac.uk/files/seminar/20130305140015152-153497.pdf"} pdf
          %p and the material here:
          %ul
            %li
              B. Fresse: Homotopy of Operads and Grothendieck-Teichmueller Groups.
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://math.univ-lille1.fr/~fresse/OperadHomotopyBook/"} Book project homepage
          %p Next here are references with more specific applications.
          %p For the perturbative quantum field theory, and for the intuition of BV formalism, see the following monograph.
          %ul
            %li K. Costello, Renormalization and effective field theory, Surveys and monographs, American Mathematical Society, 2011.
          %p For the application to topological manifold, see
          %ul
            %li
              %p [Fra] J. Francis, Factorization homology of topological manifolds, arXiv:1206.5522[math.AT].
            %li
              %p D. Ayala, J. Francis and H. Tanaka, Structured singular manifolds and factorization homology, arXiv:1206.5164[math.AT].
          %p
            On
            %math#mathml_1eede68f8c470afbdd52f909556a007fbb3d6421_34.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            space, see
          %ul
            %li [GG] R. Grady and O. Gwilliam, L-infinity spaces and derived loop spaces, arXiv:1404.5426[math.AG].
          %p On Algebraic Quantum Field Theory, see
          %ul
            %li
              %p [FR1] K. Fredenhagen and K. Rejzner, Batalin-Vilkovisky formalism in the functional approach to classical field theory, Commun.Math.Phys. 314 (2012) 93-127, arXiv:1101.5112[math-ph].
            %li
              %p [FR2] K. Fredenhagen and K. Rejzner, Batalin-Vilkovisky formalism in perturbative algebraic quantum field theory, Commun.Math.Phys. 317 (2013) 697-725, arXiv:1110.5232[math-ph].
